## Track 2: Five Edges Before the Center

**Story & Context:** At 126 BPM, the track foregrounds Edge Census. Leonor is forbidden from striking the center until five edge hits have occurred. Mara mirrors the rule by withholding the main clap until the same count completes. Each census uses a different corner order, creating subtle rotation while the underlying kick remains stable. Rui places one woodblock at every completed five-count. Tomás uses suspended-second dyads after every second center hit. Midway through, the ratio expands to 7:1, stretching anticipation while Anouk replaces the mono bass with short tongue-stopped recorder notes. The eventual center strike lands alone for half a beat before the electronics return.

