## Track 3: Back Face Holds the Rain Reading

**Story & Context:** The closer runs at 114 BPM and begins in FRONT-LEAD mode with very dry adufe attacks, one compact kick per bar, and no analog bass. After sixteen bars, Leonor rotates the drum and Mara gradually favors the rear membrane microphone, making the same patterns feel rounder and slightly more distant without changing pitch or adding reverb. Corner Debt forces every three-hit cluster to answer from the opposite side of the square. Rui flexes a metal ruler only at these reversals. In the final section, the electronics disappear one layer at a time while Rattle Residue and the rear skin remain audible. The last event is a single low center strike followed by the internal rattle settling below the sound of rain against the office windows.

